1
00:00:07,625 --> 00:00:09,025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:35,625 --> 00:01:38,865
ADAPTED FROM THE ORIGINAL WEB NOVEL
THE EARLY SPRING, BY GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:02:00,065 --> 00:02:02,025
What would you have said?

4
00:02:02,105 --> 00:02:05,065
And back then, I was craving
my dad's braised fish.

5
00:02:15,105 --> 00:02:16,185
Do not halt the project.

6
00:02:16,265 --> 00:02:17,225
Make sure everything is in order.

7
00:02:17,305 --> 00:02:18,545
I'll rush back now.

8
00:02:19,865 --> 00:02:20,745
Dad.

9
00:02:21,265 --> 00:02:22,465
I feel cold.

10
00:02:23,705 --> 00:02:24,985
I have work to do.

11
00:02:25,065 --> 00:02:26,185
Your mom will be here later.

12
00:02:26,265 --> 00:02:27,545
Call the nurse if you need anything.

13
00:03:14,065 --> 00:03:18,305
FOLLOW ME HOME

14
00:03:31,385 --> 00:03:32,985
You didn't have to come to work this soon.

15
00:03:33,825 --> 00:03:35,385
Running around won't do
your recovery any good.

16
00:03:40,865 --> 00:03:43,625
Your arm hasn't healed yet,
and you are driving.

17
00:03:45,545 --> 00:03:48,345
I use my hands to steer, not my arms.

18
00:03:52,025 --> 00:03:53,265
Shang Zhitao.

19
00:03:54,665 --> 00:03:57,225
At work, courtesy is redundant.

20
00:03:57,305 --> 00:03:59,225
It's all about an air of gravitas.

21
00:03:59,825 --> 00:04:02,145
If your opponent knows you're a pushover,

22
00:04:02,225 --> 00:04:04,465
you'll be swallowed whole.

23
00:04:05,785 --> 00:04:07,585
Noted. Thank you.

24
00:04:07,665 --> 00:04:10,025
Didn't I tell you to stop
thanking someone easily?

25
00:04:10,105 --> 00:04:11,065
Have you forgotten?

26
00:04:12,465 --> 00:04:13,905
I'll bear that in mind, Luke.

27
00:04:21,585 --> 00:04:23,745
Are you not going to ask
where we are going?

28
00:04:23,825 --> 00:04:25,385
Aren't you afraid I'll sell you out?

29
00:04:27,545 --> 00:04:29,185
I owe my life to you.

30
00:04:29,265 --> 00:04:32,185
Whatever it is, it's my treat.

31
00:04:34,745 --> 00:04:36,225
I owe my life to you too.

32
00:04:36,865 --> 00:04:38,185
How do you want me to repay it?

33
00:04:43,585 --> 00:04:45,625
I hate owing someone a favor.

34
00:04:46,425 --> 00:04:47,705
Let's just pretend
it's just you who owes me a favor.

35
00:04:51,985 --> 00:04:55,545
Then, how do you want me to repay you?

36
00:04:59,625 --> 00:05:00,585
Slowly.

37
00:05:51,665 --> 00:05:54,625
This… This is a restaurant?

38
00:05:54,705 --> 00:05:56,465
Are you afraid I'll dump your body
in the wilderness?

39
00:05:59,945 --> 00:06:04,545
BE BACK SOON

40
00:06:04,625 --> 00:06:05,585
Mian is waiting for you.

41
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:09,825
Let's go in.

42
00:06:20,585 --> 00:06:21,425
Okay.

43
00:06:25,185 --> 00:06:28,505
BE BACK SOON

44
00:06:32,705 --> 00:06:33,545
Over here.

45
00:06:40,905 --> 00:06:41,785
Careful.

46
00:08:22,265 --> 00:08:23,185
Thanks.

47
00:08:25,025 --> 00:08:26,105
Didn't you say
you were craving braised fish?

48
00:08:29,305 --> 00:08:31,585
Which one do you want? Catch it yourself.

49
00:09:41,305 --> 00:09:44,825
You must be the smart student
who doesn't need to study hard

50
00:09:44,905 --> 00:09:46,905
to get first place in your examinations.

51
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:49,505
Do you truly think
smart students never study?

52
00:09:51,345 --> 00:09:53,345
I used to think hard work would pay off,

53
00:09:53,425 --> 00:09:56,625
but I don't think so anymore.

54
00:09:57,465 --> 00:09:58,905
How's the catch?

55
00:09:59,905 --> 00:10:01,265
Did you get any fish?

56
00:10:05,505 --> 00:10:06,345
Tan Mian.

57
00:10:07,905 --> 00:10:09,225
Owner of this private restaurant.

58
00:10:09,305 --> 00:10:11,105
Also an advertisement veteran
who knows how to cook the best.

59
00:10:11,825 --> 00:10:12,665
Thank you.

60
00:10:14,625 --> 00:10:15,665
Shang Zhitao.

61
00:10:16,505 --> 00:10:18,105
-Hi, Ms. Shang.
-Hi.

62
00:10:22,665 --> 00:10:24,745
All right. Stop fishing. It's tedious.

63
00:10:24,825 --> 00:10:26,665
Ms. Shang. Which one do you want?

64
00:10:26,745 --> 00:10:28,265
I brought a net to scoop it up for you.

65
00:10:28,985 --> 00:10:32,065
Teaching one to fish
is better than giving them a fish.

66
00:10:34,265 --> 00:10:36,025
Yes. I want to catch one myself.

67
00:10:50,305 --> 00:10:52,785
Luke, thanks for teaching me how to fish.

68
00:10:52,865 --> 00:10:55,025
I now understand that
not only do I have to work hard,

69
00:10:55,105 --> 00:10:56,625
but I have to seize the right timing too.

70
00:10:56,705 --> 00:10:58,105
I didn't teach you anything.

71
00:10:58,185 --> 00:10:59,385
You learned it yourself.

72
00:11:02,545 --> 00:11:03,825
The food is ready.

73
00:11:06,505 --> 00:11:07,425
Try it.

74
00:11:07,505 --> 00:11:10,665
My secret grilled fish.

75
00:11:18,225 --> 00:11:19,465
Thank you.

76
00:11:25,825 --> 00:11:26,905
Girlfriend?

77
00:11:27,825 --> 00:11:28,825
No.

78
00:11:29,505 --> 00:11:31,825
Luke and I are colleagues.

79
00:11:33,865 --> 00:11:35,705
Does she look like my girlfriend at all?

80
00:11:36,305 --> 00:11:37,505
Right.

81
00:11:40,625 --> 00:11:43,625
Then, this colleague of yours
must be more important than a girlfriend.

82
00:11:44,785 --> 00:11:47,065
You are serving her personally.

83
00:11:48,785 --> 00:11:50,385
Focus when you're eating fish.

84
00:11:50,465 --> 00:11:51,385
Enjoy it.

85
00:11:57,865 --> 00:11:59,505
-It's nice.
-Right?

86
00:12:00,705 --> 00:12:02,425
The fish you caught
will always taste good.

87
00:12:03,545 --> 00:12:05,145
If you know how to use bait,

88
00:12:06,425 --> 00:12:07,785
you won't find yourself lacking in fish.

89
00:12:11,225 --> 00:12:13,665
Yes. We should always learn from Luke

90
00:12:13,745 --> 00:12:15,225
so that we don't become idiots.

91
00:12:18,185 --> 00:12:19,345
You hold grudges.

92
00:12:23,385 --> 00:12:24,345
Ms. Shang.

93
00:12:24,425 --> 00:12:25,545
I have a question.

94
00:12:25,625 --> 00:12:29,345
What do you think
is Luke's biggest talent?

95
00:12:31,745 --> 00:12:32,865
His creativity.

96
00:12:32,945 --> 00:12:34,905
Everyone says Luke

97
00:12:34,985 --> 00:12:37,225
is a prodigy in the advertising industry
that you can't find elsewhere.

98
00:12:39,025 --> 00:12:39,985
Prodigy?

99
00:12:41,185 --> 00:12:42,865
Ten years ago, I thought so too.

100
00:12:42,945 --> 00:12:46,345
I thought one good slogan
could leverage the entire Pacific Ocean.

101
00:12:46,425 --> 00:12:48,185
But you can generate
as much hype as you want.

102
00:12:48,265 --> 00:12:49,945
If your client's products
are not sold out,

103
00:12:50,025 --> 00:12:53,305
they won't give you the budget
to support your vision.

104
00:12:57,185 --> 00:12:58,465
See, Ms. Shang?

105
00:12:58,545 --> 00:13:01,185
His biggest talent is not creativity,

106
00:13:01,785 --> 00:13:03,145
but nitpicking.

107
00:13:04,265 --> 00:13:06,105
When he nitpicks,

108
00:13:07,185 --> 00:13:09,145
his words are more precise than a slogan.

109
00:13:12,305 --> 00:13:13,505
Dig in.

110
00:13:17,225 --> 00:13:18,705
It's probably a circuit breaker trip.

111
00:13:18,785 --> 00:13:20,265
Just eat. Let me check on it.

112
00:13:33,385 --> 00:13:34,705
How did you come in?

113
00:13:34,785 --> 00:13:35,705
You pried the lock open?

114
00:13:36,465 --> 00:13:37,705
Mr. Tan.

115
00:13:39,065 --> 00:13:39,945
Where is Luan Nian?

116
00:13:41,225 --> 00:13:42,065
Luan Nian?

117
00:13:42,145 --> 00:13:43,185
I told you he and I are no longer friends.

118
00:13:43,265 --> 00:13:45,105
We have closed. Just leave.

119
00:13:46,585 --> 00:13:48,305
How many drinks did you have?

120
00:13:48,385 --> 00:13:50,745
-I'll hail a taxi to get you home.
-I heard someone talking inside.

121
00:13:50,825 --> 00:13:51,785
-Hey you…
-You're lying to me!

122
00:13:51,865 --> 00:13:52,665
Why would I lie to you?

123
00:13:52,745 --> 00:13:54,225
Luan Nian is inside. I know it.

124
00:13:54,305 --> 00:13:55,385
-Luan Nian!
-No, he isn't.

125
00:13:55,465 --> 00:13:57,385
-It's my other friend.
-Listen. You're there, aren't you?

126
00:13:57,465 --> 00:13:58,785
Luan Nian isn't here.

127
00:13:58,865 --> 00:14:00,665
If you lie to me,
I'll burn your restaurant.

128
00:14:00,745 --> 00:14:02,225
Burn my restaurant?

129
00:14:02,305 --> 00:14:03,825
That's a crime, miss.

130
00:14:03,905 --> 00:14:05,825
Do you know
how much jail time you will get?

131
00:14:06,425 --> 00:14:07,625
Stop taking me for a fool.

132
00:14:07,705 --> 00:14:10,305
-Luan Nian! I know you're in there.
-He isn't here.

133
00:14:10,385 --> 00:14:12,585
-Don't ignore me. Come out.
-Just leave.

134
00:14:12,665 --> 00:14:14,625
-Luan Nian! Luan Nian!
-Go.

135
00:14:14,705 --> 00:14:15,785
-Careful.
-He isn't here.

136
00:14:15,865 --> 00:14:16,745
Just go.

137
00:14:16,825 --> 00:14:17,865
-Luan Nian!
-Careful.

138
00:14:17,945 --> 00:14:19,025
-Don't worry.
-Don't ignore me.

139
00:14:19,105 --> 00:14:20,025
Come out now!

140
00:14:20,105 --> 00:14:22,225
Just let me see you. We need to talk.

141
00:14:22,305 --> 00:14:24,305
Luan Nian!

142
00:14:24,385 --> 00:14:26,385
-I won't leave unless you come out.
-What happened?

143
00:14:26,465 --> 00:14:28,665
-Luan Nian!
-Something came up.

144
00:14:28,745 --> 00:14:29,945
Let's call it a day now.

145
00:14:30,025 --> 00:14:31,705
-Luan Nian.
-After she leaves,

146
00:14:31,785 --> 00:14:32,905
I'll drive you back.

147
00:14:33,425 --> 00:14:34,265
Okay.

148
00:14:43,545 --> 00:14:44,465
Luan Nian.

149
00:14:51,705 --> 00:14:53,185
I finally get to see you.

150
00:14:58,505 --> 00:14:59,585
Luan Nian.

151
00:15:00,185 --> 00:15:01,825
I'm begging you.

152
00:15:01,905 --> 00:15:03,505
Let's get back together.

153
00:15:04,465 --> 00:15:05,585
I won't be what I was before.

154
00:15:05,665 --> 00:15:06,945
I'll change.

155
00:15:09,145 --> 00:15:09,985
Zhang Xin.

156
00:15:11,305 --> 00:15:12,265
We already broke up.

157
00:15:13,425 --> 00:15:15,145
You need to accept the truth.

158
00:15:15,745 --> 00:15:17,705
There's no point in holding
onto this any longer.

159
00:15:20,345 --> 00:15:21,425
No point?

160
00:15:23,745 --> 00:15:26,345
For you, I argued with my parents,

161
00:15:27,665 --> 00:15:29,905
gave up everything I had in the US,
and returned to Beijing.

162
00:15:31,065 --> 00:15:33,705
-Is that nothing in your eyes?
-You made the decision yourself.

163
00:15:34,305 --> 00:15:35,905
Don't pin that on me.

164
00:15:36,745 --> 00:15:39,305
We both chose to break up.

165
00:15:39,385 --> 00:15:40,745
It's been a year.

166
00:15:41,665 --> 00:15:42,985
You've been texting, calling,
and stalking me.

167
00:15:43,065 --> 00:15:44,425
Enough is enough.

168
00:15:44,505 --> 00:15:45,585
It's time to put an end to this.

169
00:15:46,625 --> 00:15:48,785
I am having a private moment
with my friend.

170
00:15:48,865 --> 00:15:50,145
Please leave.

171
00:15:54,025 --> 00:15:55,425
Your friend?

172
00:15:55,505 --> 00:15:57,345
Don't deny it.

173
00:15:57,425 --> 00:15:58,505
She's your new love interest.

174
00:16:06,945 --> 00:16:08,945
Relationships go through ups and downs.

175
00:16:09,025 --> 00:16:10,305
We broke up.

176
00:16:11,145 --> 00:16:13,105
So, I'll just wait
until you break up with her.

177
00:16:15,385 --> 00:16:17,065
When did you two get together?

178
00:16:21,025 --> 00:16:22,105
You misunderstood.

179
00:16:22,665 --> 00:16:24,025
We're just co-workers.

180
00:16:24,705 --> 00:16:26,185
This is between us.

181
00:16:26,785 --> 00:16:28,065
Do not involve other people.

182
00:16:32,465 --> 00:16:33,425
Go inside first.

183
00:16:35,145 --> 00:16:36,145
-Don't come near me!
-Zhang Xin.

184
00:16:36,225 --> 00:16:37,425
-Don't come near me.
-Drop it.

185
00:16:37,505 --> 00:16:38,745
Calm down.

186
00:16:40,105 --> 00:16:41,545
Don't do anything reckless.

187
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:43,225
Put the knife down now.

188
00:16:43,305 --> 00:16:44,505
Leave this place.

189
00:16:44,585 --> 00:16:45,825
I'll pretend nothing happened here.

190
00:16:45,905 --> 00:16:47,625
I already called the police.

191
00:16:59,465 --> 00:17:00,985
I love you so much.

192
00:17:03,705 --> 00:17:05,865
Yet you go and love someone else.

193
00:17:10,865 --> 00:17:12,865
Calm down. Put the knife down.

194
00:17:16,385 --> 00:17:18,944
You know what? Let's talk. Okay?

195
00:17:19,985 --> 00:17:21,265
Tell me.

196
00:17:22,424 --> 00:17:23,464
What did I do wrong?

197
00:17:26,345 --> 00:17:27,745
I think you need treatment.

198
00:17:28,265 --> 00:17:29,785
I'll go with you to see a therapist.

199
00:17:29,865 --> 00:17:30,905
No.

200
00:17:31,625 --> 00:17:33,505
You used to call me a control freak.

201
00:17:34,545 --> 00:17:36,185
You think I'm sick, don't you?

202
00:17:36,265 --> 00:17:38,305
-You think I'm crazy?
-No, I do not.

203
00:17:39,385 --> 00:17:40,905
But you cannot
let this obsession continue.

204
00:17:41,425 --> 00:17:42,185
Give me the knife.

205
00:17:43,985 --> 00:17:45,465
-Are you okay, Luan Nian?
-Are you out of your mind?

206
00:17:46,185 --> 00:17:47,025
‎Luan Nian…

207
00:17:48,985 --> 00:17:49,825
I'm fine.

208
00:17:50,825 --> 00:17:52,065
-I…
-Again?

209
00:17:52,145 --> 00:17:53,505
Are you okay?

210
00:18:00,745 --> 00:18:03,145
Stop her.

211
00:18:23,265 --> 00:18:24,185
Ms. Shang.

212
00:18:24,865 --> 00:18:26,865
-You must have been terrified.
-No.

213
00:18:28,265 --> 00:18:30,025
Please don't misunderstand.

214
00:18:30,665 --> 00:18:32,945
They only dated briefly,

215
00:18:33,025 --> 00:18:34,465
and they broke up a long time ago.

216
00:18:34,545 --> 00:18:36,065
I can reassure you

217
00:18:36,145 --> 00:18:38,825
that Luke would never two-time anyone.

218
00:18:38,905 --> 00:18:40,185
No, you have the wrong idea.

219
00:18:40,265 --> 00:18:41,945
We really are just colleagues.

220
00:18:42,025 --> 00:18:43,345
He's my superior.

221
00:18:43,425 --> 00:18:48,145
Then, you're the first co-worker
he brought to my restaurant.

222
00:18:52,625 --> 00:18:54,505
That's because he has helped me a lot.

223
00:18:54,585 --> 00:18:57,225
I wanted to buy him a meal to thank him.

224
00:18:59,105 --> 00:19:02,465
Perhaps you didn't know
that Luke and I were co-workers once too.

225
00:19:03,665 --> 00:19:06,345
In one year, I closed deals
worth 80 million yuan.

226
00:19:06,425 --> 00:19:07,945
Yet he never bought me dinner.

227
00:19:08,545 --> 00:19:11,505
Did you use to work in Lime too?

228
00:19:11,585 --> 00:19:12,505
No.

229
00:19:12,585 --> 00:19:14,505
Luke and I worked together
before he went to Lime.

230
00:19:15,385 --> 00:19:17,985
He used to own
his own advertising company.

231
00:19:18,065 --> 00:19:19,105
I worked under him.

232
00:19:20,545 --> 00:19:22,745
Why did you two quit then?

233
00:19:24,265 --> 00:19:25,465
We lost the drive.

234
00:19:26,065 --> 00:19:27,465
In all those years,

235
00:19:27,545 --> 00:19:29,985
we encountered many unreasonable clients.

236
00:19:30,745 --> 00:19:32,665
Every day, our work could not be finished.

237
00:19:33,265 --> 00:19:34,945
People couldn't be reasoned with.

238
00:19:35,025 --> 00:19:36,145
They blew hot and cold.

239
00:19:36,225 --> 00:19:40,225
And we spent every day carrying out
useless communication.

240
00:19:41,145 --> 00:19:43,025
I quit. I was tired.

241
00:19:44,905 --> 00:19:47,425
Why didn't he continue then?

242
00:19:48,025 --> 00:19:50,545
Do not ever mention
his company before him.

243
00:19:50,625 --> 00:19:51,705
He'll scowl at you.

244
00:19:53,145 --> 00:19:55,385
We were betrayed by one of our own.

245
00:19:56,305 --> 00:19:57,545
Luke was seriously affected by it.

246
00:19:58,665 --> 00:20:01,225
Besides, his family prohibited him
from starting his own business.

247
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:02,865
What were you guys talking about?

248
00:20:04,985 --> 00:20:06,305
How's your hand?

249
00:20:06,385 --> 00:20:07,345
I'm fine.

250
00:20:07,425 --> 00:20:09,265
The doctor said not to wet the wound.

251
00:20:09,345 --> 00:20:10,185
Be mindful of that.

252
00:20:12,185 --> 00:20:13,505
I'll leave you two be then.

253
00:20:13,585 --> 00:20:14,545
I'll bring the car over.

254
00:20:20,585 --> 00:20:21,825
Come. We'll drive you home.

255
00:20:22,345 --> 00:20:23,745
I already hailed a taxi.

256
00:20:24,345 --> 00:20:25,505
You two are leaving now?

257
00:20:25,585 --> 00:20:26,465
Are you not going to look after her?

258
00:20:27,665 --> 00:20:29,105
Why should I?

259
00:20:29,825 --> 00:20:31,345
I already informed her family.

260
00:20:34,945 --> 00:20:37,185
You must think
I'm an irresponsible playboy.

261
00:20:38,425 --> 00:20:39,665
No.

262
00:20:39,745 --> 00:20:42,905
Relationships can be messy
and complicated.

263
00:20:43,905 --> 00:20:44,825
Worry not.

264
00:20:44,905 --> 00:20:46,945
I won't tell anyone. I swear.

265
00:20:48,665 --> 00:20:50,385
I do not believe in vows.

266
00:20:51,105 --> 00:20:53,025
And I don't care about others' opinions.

267
00:20:53,105 --> 00:20:54,145
She and I already broke up.

268
00:20:55,225 --> 00:20:56,905
When two people first get together,

269
00:20:56,985 --> 00:20:58,585
I think they often share the same goal.

270
00:20:58,665 --> 00:21:00,625
But as time goes by,
people might change their minds.

271
00:21:00,705 --> 00:21:03,985
It's no one's fault
if the relationship falls apart.

272
00:21:04,065 --> 00:21:05,025
People want different things, that's all.

273
00:21:05,105 --> 00:21:07,785
She chose to hold onto it,
and you chose to let go.

274
00:21:07,865 --> 00:21:08,745
There's no right or wrong.

275
00:21:09,345 --> 00:21:10,985
So you're saying
I should keep entangling with her,

276
00:21:11,065 --> 00:21:12,625
even though I no longer love her.

277
00:21:13,505 --> 00:21:15,265
No, I didn't say that.

278
00:21:16,145 --> 00:21:20,505
I just think that love shouldn't
make one this miserable.

279
00:21:22,905 --> 00:21:24,145
How many relationships have you had?

280
00:21:25,905 --> 00:21:28,025
Just one.

281
00:21:28,625 --> 00:21:29,625
How was the breakup?

282
00:21:30,865 --> 00:21:32,865
A reluctant separation
with mutual blessings?

283
00:21:33,665 --> 00:21:36,665
We had good intentions
when we got together,

284
00:21:36,745 --> 00:21:39,745
and we didn't break up unhappily.

285
00:21:42,385 --> 00:21:44,505
You're quite mature when it comes to love.

286
00:21:50,105 --> 00:21:52,225
I… I think my taxi is here.

287
00:21:52,305 --> 00:21:53,345
Let me check.

288
00:22:24,905 --> 00:22:26,105
Tao.

289
00:22:26,185 --> 00:22:27,345
How come you're back?

290
00:22:27,905 --> 00:22:30,025
Want to hang out tonight?

291
00:22:30,105 --> 00:22:31,185
I can't.

292
00:22:31,265 --> 00:22:33,185
I need to brush up on my English.

293
00:22:33,265 --> 00:22:34,505
My colleagues all studied abroad.

294
00:22:34,585 --> 00:22:35,825
I don't want to fall too far behind.

295
00:22:35,905 --> 00:22:39,345
-You go ahead.
-You stay at home all the time.

296
00:22:39,425 --> 00:22:41,505
You've been studying every day
during your days off.

297
00:22:41,585 --> 00:22:43,745
You're affecting my after-work life.

298
00:22:44,265 --> 00:22:45,105
All of you are here.

299
00:22:46,145 --> 00:22:47,545
You should go out and relax.

300
00:22:47,625 --> 00:22:48,465
It's Friday today.

301
00:22:49,225 --> 00:22:51,225
I'm dumb, so I have to work harder.

302
00:22:52,985 --> 00:22:55,145
Oh. My friends invited me to play the game
Legends of the Three Kingdoms later.

303
00:22:55,225 --> 00:22:56,185
Do you want to join us?

304
00:22:57,305 --> 00:22:58,585
What did I just say?

305
00:22:58,665 --> 00:23:00,265
Friday is meant for fun.

306
00:23:00,345 --> 00:23:02,105
LTK or the bar.

307
00:23:02,185 --> 00:23:03,265
Pick one.

308
00:23:03,345 --> 00:23:04,585
Neither.

309
00:23:09,185 --> 00:23:10,185
Talk some sense into her.

310
00:23:12,385 --> 00:23:15,745
Oh. I fixed this one. Take this.

311
00:23:20,625 --> 00:23:22,705
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

312
00:23:27,345 --> 00:23:29,025
Stop hesitating, Tao.

313
00:23:29,105 --> 00:23:31,585
Sun's friends must be very smart.

314
00:23:31,665 --> 00:23:33,505
Let's go meet some quality people.

315
00:23:33,585 --> 00:23:35,025
It's just studying
in a different place, right?

316
00:23:35,625 --> 00:23:36,825
So that's a deal then. I'll get changed.

317
00:23:36,905 --> 00:23:37,905
Hurry up.

318
00:23:37,985 --> 00:23:39,065
I changed my mind. I'll wear this.

319
00:23:39,145 --> 00:23:40,145
It's pretty.

320
00:23:53,225 --> 00:23:55,345
-Let me check on my cards.
-That's rough, buddy.

321
00:23:55,425 --> 00:23:56,985
Wait, how does "Kill" work?

322
00:23:57,065 --> 00:23:58,185
-Can I just use "Dodge" to get out of it?
-Hello!

323
00:23:58,265 --> 00:24:00,185
-It's rare that Sun is willing to come out
-Hello.

324
00:24:00,265 --> 00:24:01,465
and he brought
two beautiful girls with him.

325
00:24:02,665 --> 00:24:03,785
Introduce them to us.

326
00:24:04,465 --> 00:24:07,385
I am Sun Yu.
You can call me Yu or Dabaoyu.

327
00:24:07,985 --> 00:24:08,985
Hello.

328
00:24:09,065 --> 00:24:10,025
This is Tao.

329
00:24:10,105 --> 00:24:11,225
-Shang Zhitao.
-Hello.

330
00:24:11,305 --> 00:24:12,985
-Take a seat.
-Come.

331
00:24:13,065 --> 00:24:14,945
-The drinks are here.
-Careful.

332
00:24:16,705 --> 00:24:19,065
-Thanks.
-Hello.

333
00:24:19,145 --> 00:24:21,225
My name is Long Zhentian.

334
00:24:22,265 --> 00:24:23,585
Your Chinese is so good.

335
00:24:23,665 --> 00:24:25,065
I am Feng Qiuhuang.

336
00:24:26,585 --> 00:24:28,465
-Shang Zhitao.
-Hi.

337
00:24:28,545 --> 00:24:31,305
Zhentian is my batchmate
from the university. He's Canadian.

338
00:24:31,385 --> 00:24:33,345
His native languages
are English and French,

339
00:24:33,425 --> 00:24:34,905
and he speaks really good Chinese.

340
00:24:35,745 --> 00:24:36,945
I can tell.

341
00:24:37,025 --> 00:24:39,225
You like playing LTK as a foreigner?

342
00:24:39,305 --> 00:24:41,545
So-so. The third best player in the world.

343
00:24:45,465 --> 00:24:49,945
I'm actually looking for a Chinese tutor
to practice my speaking skills.

344
00:24:50,025 --> 00:24:51,265
You're looking for a Chinese tutor?

345
00:24:51,985 --> 00:24:55,185
What a coincidence.
Tao is looking for an English tutor.

346
00:24:55,265 --> 00:24:58,265
You two can exchange numbers
and study with one another.

347
00:24:58,345 --> 00:25:00,825
Wonderful. Give me a call.

348
00:25:01,425 --> 00:25:02,265
Type your number.

349
00:25:03,385 --> 00:25:06,025
What's your goal
for your English proficiency?

350
00:25:06,745 --> 00:25:09,585
As good as your Chinese proficiency.

351
00:25:10,385 --> 00:25:12,305
Then, you'll have to work hard.

352
00:25:12,385 --> 00:25:14,305
You too.

353
00:25:14,385 --> 00:25:15,905
All right. Enough serious talk.

354
00:25:15,985 --> 00:25:17,425
-Deal the cards now.
-Deal the cards.

355
00:25:17,505 --> 00:25:19,185
Here. Take this.

356
00:25:33,265 --> 00:25:34,105
Come in.

357
00:25:35,345 --> 00:25:37,745
Boss. I'm leaving now.

358
00:25:43,345 --> 00:25:45,145
It's Friday today.

359
00:25:45,225 --> 00:25:46,985
You don't live to work.

360
00:25:48,545 --> 00:25:49,745
It's only 7 p.m.

361
00:25:49,825 --> 00:25:51,305
But it's the weekend now.

362
00:25:51,385 --> 00:25:53,785
A normal person would already
be queuing at a hot pot restaurant.

363
00:25:53,865 --> 00:25:55,105
Just go.

364
00:25:55,665 --> 00:25:56,505
Happy weekend.

365
00:25:57,305 --> 00:25:58,305
Do go home early.

366
00:26:14,625 --> 00:26:17,905
It seems Yuanzhu has been charmed.

367
00:26:18,545 --> 00:26:19,785
-Allow me.
-Mince your words now.

368
00:26:19,865 --> 00:26:21,705
-Thanks.
-If Sun gets mad,

369
00:26:21,785 --> 00:26:23,225
he'll kill your character off.

370
00:26:23,305 --> 00:26:25,785
Sun has a good temper. He won't kill you.

371
00:26:25,865 --> 00:26:27,545
You don't know this.

372
00:26:27,625 --> 00:26:29,625
Back then, our boss stole his code

373
00:26:30,505 --> 00:26:32,185
and even tried to pin
the blame on him and fire him.

374
00:26:32,265 --> 00:26:33,905
And he just flipped the table.

375
00:26:33,985 --> 00:26:35,665
I didn't know
you could be this aggressive.

376
00:26:36,345 --> 00:26:37,585
You're always so even-tempered.

377
00:26:37,665 --> 00:26:40,145
That guy must have been very awful
to make you this angry.

378
00:26:40,225 --> 00:26:43,225
Guess what happened next?

379
00:26:43,305 --> 00:26:47,105
That jerk couldn't understand
the logic behind Zhu's code.

380
00:26:47,185 --> 00:26:49,785
There was a bug, and he couldn't fix it.

381
00:26:49,865 --> 00:26:53,425
So he came crawling back
and begged Zhu to come back.

382
00:26:53,505 --> 00:26:55,665
You should've seen the face of that loser.

383
00:26:55,745 --> 00:27:00,785
Well, Zhu, what did you tell him?

384
00:27:03,185 --> 00:27:06,865
I told him that at work,
nothing was a given.

385
00:27:06,945 --> 00:27:08,425
No one should think that
they are above everyone else.

386
00:27:09,385 --> 00:27:12,065
Without the effort of the employees,

387
00:27:12,145 --> 00:27:13,705
no matter how big the company is,

388
00:27:13,785 --> 00:27:15,865
it's just an empty shell.

389
00:27:15,945 --> 00:27:17,185
Don't lie.

390
00:27:17,265 --> 00:27:19,825
What you wanted to say was…

391
00:27:23,705 --> 00:27:25,025
Screw you!

392
00:27:30,385 --> 00:27:31,225
Come. Carry on.

393
00:27:31,305 --> 00:27:32,145
-Come.
-It's your turn now.

394
00:27:32,225 --> 00:27:33,785
I use Invasion of Nanman.

395
00:27:40,465 --> 00:27:42,505
-I don't have any strike cards.
-Strike cards.

396
00:27:42,585 --> 00:27:43,625
I don't have any strike cards.

397
00:27:43,705 --> 00:27:44,905
I still have one, Tao.

398
00:27:46,465 --> 00:27:48,105
Sun Yu. They are having an event here.

399
00:27:48,185 --> 00:27:49,465
Where are you?

400
00:27:49,545 --> 00:27:51,225
Come now. Quick.

401
00:27:51,945 --> 00:27:54,625
Okay. Sure. I'll be there.

402
00:27:55,145 --> 00:27:56,025
Okay.

403
00:27:58,705 --> 00:27:59,545
Sorry, guys.

404
00:27:59,625 --> 00:28:03,105
My boss told me
something happened at the event.

405
00:28:03,185 --> 00:28:05,065
I need to head back to fix it.

406
00:28:05,145 --> 00:28:07,265
I have to go now.
I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.

407
00:28:07,345 --> 00:28:09,305
My company can't live without me.

408
00:28:09,385 --> 00:28:10,825
I have to go now.

409
00:28:10,905 --> 00:28:12,305
-Bye.
-Take care.

410
00:28:12,385 --> 00:28:14,345
It's hard to get a ride here.
I'll drive you out.

411
00:28:15,265 --> 00:28:16,305
-Okay.
-Let's go.

412
00:28:16,385 --> 00:28:17,265
Come.

413
00:28:17,825 --> 00:28:19,305
It's getting late.
Let's head back as well.

414
00:28:19,385 --> 00:28:20,585
-Okay.
-Okay.

415
00:28:20,665 --> 00:28:21,665
We'll hang out another time.

416
00:28:21,745 --> 00:28:23,145
-See you.
-Bye.

417
00:28:23,225 --> 00:28:24,745
-Bye.
-We'll go as well.

418
00:28:24,825 --> 00:28:26,265
-Bye.
-Bye.

419
00:28:29,985 --> 00:28:32,665
Are you free later?

420
00:28:32,745 --> 00:28:33,665
Do you have time?

421
00:28:33,745 --> 00:28:36,105
Maybe we can have our first session today?

422
00:28:37,145 --> 00:28:38,265
Really?

423
00:28:38,345 --> 00:28:39,225
Yes.

424
00:28:39,825 --> 00:28:41,425
Should we go somewhere else?

425
00:28:42,105 --> 00:28:43,425
-Sure.
-Okay.

426
00:28:43,945 --> 00:28:44,905
Let me pack this up.

427
00:28:52,305 --> 00:28:53,025
‎Hello.

428
00:28:53,105 --> 00:28:54,305
Where are you?

429
00:28:54,385 --> 00:28:55,465
About to drive home.

430
00:28:55,545 --> 00:28:57,305
Song Qiuhan and Chen Kuannian are back.

431
00:28:57,385 --> 00:28:58,625
Let's grab a drink today.

432
00:28:58,705 --> 00:29:00,105
-Their bar is launching today.
-No, thanks.

433
00:29:00,785 --> 00:29:02,505
Dude. It's the weekend.

434
00:29:02,585 --> 00:29:05,265
Are you really going to stay at home
and talk to your fish?

435
00:29:05,945 --> 00:29:07,585
That's my time with my pet.

436
00:29:08,345 --> 00:29:09,225
Fine.

437
00:29:09,305 --> 00:29:12,385
If I cannot convince you,
the others will call you anyway.

438
00:29:12,465 --> 00:29:13,905
Find a way to turn them down then.

439
00:29:13,985 --> 00:29:15,025
Hanging up.

440
00:29:33,545 --> 00:29:34,665
This is the place.

441
00:29:34,745 --> 00:29:35,825
It's new.

442
00:29:35,905 --> 00:29:39,185
I heard there's
a special performance tonight.

443
00:29:39,265 --> 00:29:40,785
It's crowded.

444
00:29:41,785 --> 00:29:44,185
Drifters in Beijing all gather here.

445
00:29:44,265 --> 00:29:45,865
It's the culture.

446
00:29:45,945 --> 00:29:46,985
The culture.

447
00:29:58,065 --> 00:30:00,625
This is the soul of Beijing.

448
00:30:00,705 --> 00:30:01,905
You work during the day.

449
00:30:01,985 --> 00:30:04,265
You live at night.

450
00:30:04,345 --> 00:30:05,585
It is quite different.

451
00:30:05,665 --> 00:30:07,545
When I first came to Beijing,

452
00:30:07,625 --> 00:30:09,705
I could not speak a word of Chinese.

453
00:30:09,785 --> 00:30:12,945
I learned it all from friends
I made in bars.

454
00:30:13,025 --> 00:30:14,625
It's the same with English.

455
00:30:14,705 --> 00:30:16,225
You can't rely on textbooks alone.

456
00:30:16,305 --> 00:30:17,785
You must come here

457
00:30:17,865 --> 00:30:21,185
and be immersed
in a real language environment.

458
00:30:22,425 --> 00:30:23,745
Let me teach you how to order a drink.

459
00:30:30,105 --> 00:30:31,025
Qiuhan.

460
00:30:31,105 --> 00:30:32,745
How much did you invest in this place?

461
00:30:34,785 --> 00:30:36,305
-How much?
-Chen Kuannian invested in it as well.

462
00:30:36,385 --> 00:30:37,625
-We're in it together.
-What do you think?

463
00:30:38,705 --> 00:30:39,585
I invested in it too.

464
00:30:40,865 --> 00:30:42,545
You two sure are rich.

465
00:30:42,625 --> 00:30:44,225
It is good.

466
00:30:44,305 --> 00:30:45,305
This place is not bad, right?

467
00:30:45,385 --> 00:30:47,025
-But your decor is…
-Decor is…

468
00:30:47,105 --> 00:30:48,705
The location is good.

469
00:31:05,185 --> 00:31:06,985
Is that you, Mr. Luan?

470
00:31:07,065 --> 00:31:08,305
Your fish finally let you out?

471
00:31:09,225 --> 00:31:10,425
Luan Nian?

472
00:31:11,505 --> 00:31:12,385
Let him out?

473
00:31:12,465 --> 00:31:14,265
I bet his fish is sick of him,

474
00:31:14,345 --> 00:31:15,905
so it kicked him out.

475
00:31:16,945 --> 00:31:19,265
Since you're here,
then we must have a drink.

476
00:31:19,345 --> 00:31:20,465
It's on you.

477
00:31:20,545 --> 00:31:21,585
Consider it your gift for my opening day.

478
00:31:21,665 --> 00:31:23,585
Don't. I just paid it.

479
00:31:23,665 --> 00:31:25,105
As you should.

480
00:31:25,185 --> 00:31:26,305
-Come.
-Come.

481
00:31:29,585 --> 00:31:30,585
Hello.

482
00:31:43,785 --> 00:31:45,265
You need to work on your pronunciation.

483
00:31:54,385 --> 00:31:55,145
Yes.

484
00:32:05,025 --> 00:32:06,745
You said two martinis ten times.

485
00:32:06,825 --> 00:32:07,745
That's 20 martinis.

486
00:32:18,305 --> 00:32:20,905
Long Zhentian. We'll split the bill.

487
00:32:22,505 --> 00:32:23,665
Okay.

488
00:32:23,745 --> 00:32:25,985
Then, I'll teach you more things today.

489
00:32:26,065 --> 00:32:26,905
What do you want to learn?

490
00:32:28,065 --> 00:32:31,865
I want to learn how to politely
turn down drinks during a business dinner.

491
00:32:32,865 --> 00:32:33,785
But…

492
00:32:33,865 --> 00:32:35,505
You're Chinese,

493
00:32:35,585 --> 00:32:36,465
and you work in advertising.

494
00:32:36,545 --> 00:32:38,625
How are you supposed
to close deals without drinking?

495
00:32:39,905 --> 00:32:40,865
Even you say so.

496
00:32:40,945 --> 00:32:44,105
So, how do I learn to hold my drinks?

497
00:32:44,185 --> 00:32:45,465
Just drink more.

498
00:32:45,545 --> 00:32:46,865
-Really?
-Yes.

499
00:32:55,065 --> 00:32:58,385
Maybe recite some Chinese poems or idioms.

500
00:32:58,465 --> 00:32:59,665
It'll be even better.

501
00:32:59,745 --> 00:33:01,945
Quick. Teach me something.

502
00:33:04,145 --> 00:33:05,825
What makes you drunk
is not liquor, but desires.

503
00:33:06,585 --> 00:33:08,985
What makes you drunk
is not liquor, but desires.

504
00:33:09,065 --> 00:33:12,345
But sorrows feel even more bitter
when you drown them with liquor.

505
00:33:12,425 --> 00:33:16,625
But sorrows feel even more bitter
when you drown them with liquor.

506
00:33:16,705 --> 00:33:18,425
Yes. Cheers.

507
00:33:18,505 --> 00:33:19,465
Cheers.

508
00:33:26,585 --> 00:33:29,745
Luke. We haven't heard you sing in years.

509
00:33:29,825 --> 00:33:31,105
It's our opening day today.

510
00:33:31,185 --> 00:33:32,585
Sing for us.

511
00:33:32,665 --> 00:33:33,745
No way.

512
00:33:33,825 --> 00:33:35,625
Don't say no.

513
00:33:35,705 --> 00:33:37,105
Everyone is here.

514
00:33:37,185 --> 00:33:38,025
It's our bar.

515
00:33:38,105 --> 00:33:39,265
You won't embarrass yourself.

516
00:33:40,705 --> 00:33:41,625
No.

517
00:33:41,705 --> 00:33:43,905
You're still the same
as when you were at school.

518
00:33:43,985 --> 00:33:44,825
You don't play along.

519
00:33:44,905 --> 00:33:50,185
Just get off your pedestal
and let us enjoy your talent.

520
00:34:06,905 --> 00:34:07,865
Will I get paid?

521
00:34:08,545 --> 00:34:09,744
-I…
-Yes.

522
00:34:10,385 --> 00:34:11,824
When we were studying…

523
00:34:11,905 --> 00:34:13,065
-How much was it again?
-500 yuan.

524
00:34:13,145 --> 00:34:13,985
-Yes, 500 yuan.
-Yes, 500 yuan.

525
00:34:14,065 --> 00:34:15,665
I'll pay you ten times that amount. No.

526
00:34:15,744 --> 00:34:20,304
If you can sing until morning,
I'll give this bar to you.

527
00:34:21,545 --> 00:34:23,065
You might as well earn it.

528
00:34:29,465 --> 00:34:31,304
-Seriously?
-Here he goes.

529
00:34:31,385 --> 00:34:32,304
He's doing it.

530
00:34:32,824 --> 00:34:33,905
Gosh!

531
00:34:36,824 --> 00:34:38,065
Yes!

532
00:34:50,985 --> 00:34:54,425
Do you think Luan Nian
is quite distracted today?

533
00:34:54,505 --> 00:34:55,784
What is he looking at?

534
00:34:55,865 --> 00:34:57,225
Impossible.

535
00:34:57,305 --> 00:35:00,225
Who is this beauty who earns his gaze?

536
00:35:02,145 --> 00:35:03,785
I think I know that girl.

537
00:35:03,865 --> 00:35:05,385
